      "updated_at": "2018-09-19T02:30:24Z",
      "body": "A little late to this thread but option 1 seems like a good option. It's worth distinguishing between accuracy and precision. What we are really recording with `accuracy` is \"precision\" even if we provide 12 decimal places due to limitations of GPS the accuracy of those readings will probably be less because of factors that effect GPS like urban canyon.\r\n\r\nGood  [StackExchange thread](https://gis.stackexchange.com/questions/8650/measuring-accuracy-of-latitude-and-longitude) on the subject.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
