      "created_at": "2018-09-19T18:55:54Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-19T18:55:54Z",
      "body": "I agree that we don't want to conflate imprecision due to the fundamentals of GPS sensors (called `accuracy` on both major smartphone platforms) with intentional lowering of precision via truncation or snapping. \r\n\r\nImagine a tool that processes MDS entities -- that tool should be able to know whether it's working with a stream of GPS locations, a list of census tract centroids, or a list of locations snapped to a 1km grid. (just 2 examples)",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
