      "created_at": "2019-05-21T23:32:45Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-05-21T23:43:28Z",
      "body": "Could one version of the specification just take block level aggregations to a [SharedStreets ](https://github.com/sharedstreets/sharedstreets-ref-system) ID or OSM ID? I realize this is an old thread but, I think this provides the degree of operational data many cities would need for curbside management and related applications. I think route choice applications might be lost, but this might be a problem that requires a tiers of deployment perhaps?\r\n\r\nI agree with @aickin  that this could be compatible with by snapping all points to the the nearest \"centroid\" of a SS ID or OSM ID. Benefit of these is that in theory they should be able to be internationally compatible if based around OSM. \r\n\r\nMy only concern here is it might not be \"anonymized\" enough.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
